K-means WCSS: 4.000000.

| merge | child_a | child_b | height | sse_increase | cumulative_sse |
| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| 0 | 0 | 1 | 2.000000 | 2 | 2 |
| 1 | 2 | 3 | 2.000000 | 2 | 4 |
| 2 | 4 | 5 | 11.313708 | 64 | 68 |

\image(figures/clustering_iris_four_points.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Known means and merge costs connect K-means inertia to the native Ward-height normalization.)
\alttext(The left panel groups four points around centres one and nine. The right shows the three-merge Ward tree. A table gives both child ids, heights, squared-error increments and cumulative squared error.)

>> A density chain has cores, borders and a rejected point

Two chains at (0,.1,.2,.3) and (1.5,1.6,1.7,1.8), plus an isolated point at
three, use epsilon=.11 and min_samples=3. In each chain, the two interior points see
three observations including themselves, while endpoints see two. The interiors are
core and endpoints are border: all four join, even though each chain's diameter .3
exceeds epsilon. The isolated point is noise. A radius sweep starts with no cores,
creates two components, then joins them and absorbs the last point.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/clustering_iris_density.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  using namespace dm::stats;
  dm::dstruct::DataFrame d;
  d.add_column("x", std::vector<double>{0, .1, .2, .3, 1.5, 1.6, 1.7, 1.8, 3});
  d.add_column("display_y", std::vector<double>(9, 0));
  DBSCANOptions o;
  o.eps         = .11;
  o.min_samples = 3;
  const DBSCAN fit(d, {"x"}, o);
  if (fit.n_clusters() != 2 || fit.n_noise() != 1 || fit.labels()[0] != fit.labels()[3])
    throw std::runtime_error("density reference mismatch");
  auto projection =
      plot_clusters(d, "x", "display_y", fit.labels(), "Core chains absorb their borders");
  projection.y_limits(-.5, 1.5);
  std::vector<double> eps = {.05, .11, 1.21, 3}, clusters, noise;
  for (double radius : eps) {
    o.eps = radius;
    const DBSCAN m(d, {"x"}, o);
    clusters.push_back(m.n_clusters());
    noise.push_back(m.n_noise());
  }
  auto sweep = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  sweep.line(eps, clusters, "clusters", {37, 99, 235})
      .points(eps, clusters, "counts", {37, 99, 235}, 4)
      .line(eps, noise, "noise rows", {220, 38, 38})
      .title("Radius creates, then joins components")
      .x_label("epsilon")
      .y_label("count")
      .y_limits(0, 12);
  dm::dstruct::DataFrame t;
  t.add_column("epsilon", eps);
  t.add_column("clusters", clusters);
  t.add_column("noise_rows", noise);
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2)
      .add(projection)
      .add(sweep)
      .size(1100, 490)
      .fit_panels()
      .save_svg("build/clustering_iris_density.svg");
  std::print("{}\n", t.to_md(3));
}
```
