\image(figures/clustering_iris_kmeans.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Petal plots display the fitted four-dimensional partition; the species labels are a separate post-fit reference.)
\alttext(Two panels show petal length versus width coloured by true species and by fitted K-means group. Tables give species means and per-cluster size, majority class, majority count and purity, followed by WCSS and adjusted Rand.)

>> Cluster-count and restart sweeps answer different questions

The k=1..8 curve uses twenty restarts per fit, without species labels.
WCSS usually decreases as more centres represent the same data; it is not comparable
across different feature scalings. The second panel keeps k=3 fixed and extends one
seeded restart stream from one through twenty runs. Its best objective cannot increase,
because every shorter candidate set is a prefix of the next. A flat curve here would
mean the first seed already found the best observed basin, not that restarts are
unnecessary on arbitrary data. Neither curve identifies a uniquely correct k.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/clustering_iris_sweeps.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  using namespace dm::stats;
  const auto                     d = dm::datasets::iris();
  const std::vector<std::string> f = {"Sepal.Length", "Sepal.Width", "Petal.Length", "Petal.Width"};
  std::vector<double>            k, inertia;
  for (int c = 1; c <= 8; ++c) {
    KMeansOptions o;
    o.n_clusters = c;
    o.n_init     = 20;
    const KMeans m(d, f, o);
    k.push_back(c);
    inertia.push_back(m.inertia());
  }
  std::vector<double> runs = {1, 2, 5, 10, 20}, best;
  for (double count : runs) {
    KMeansOptions o;
    o.n_clusters = 3;
    o.n_init     = std::size_t(count);
    best.push_back(KMeans(d, f, o).inertia());
  }
  for (std::size_t i = 1; i < best.size(); ++i)
    if (best[i] > best[i - 1] + 1e-10)
      throw std::runtime_error("restart-prefix objective worsened");
  dm::dstruct::DataFrame a, b;
  a.add_column("k", k);
  a.add_column("wcss", inertia);
  b.add_column("restarts", runs);
  b.add_column("best_wcss_k3", best);
  auto elbow = dm::graphics::RPlot::create(), restarts = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  elbow.line(k, inertia, "WCSS", {37, 99, 235})
      .points(k, inertia, "fits", {37, 99, 235}, 4)
      .title("More centres reduce representation error")
      .x_label("requested clusters k")
      .y_label("WCSS (cm squared)")
      .y_limits(0, 900);
  restarts.line(runs, best, "best WCSS", {220, 38, 38})
      .points(runs, best, "prefixes", {220, 38, 38}, 4)
      .title("Best of a growing restart prefix")
      .x_label("K-means++ restarts, seed 42")
      .y_label("WCSS at k = 3")
      .y_limits(78.7, 80);
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2)
      .add(elbow)
      .add(restarts)
      .size(1100, 490)
      .fit_panels()
      .save_svg("build/clustering_iris_sweeps.svg");
  std::print("{}\n\n{}\n", a.to_md(9), b.to_md(9));
}
```
